	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## Setup

Download the languages you want to translate in System Settings → General → Language &amp; Region → Translation Languages. Translation runs entirely on-device, so a language is unavailable until its model is on disk. Type `?` after the keyword to see which languages are ready.

## Usage

Translate text between two languages without a network connection via the `t` keyword. The direction is detected automatically, so the same keyword works both ways.

![Translating a phrase](images/translate.jpeg)

* &lt;kbd&gt;↩︎&lt;/kbd&gt; Copy the translation to the clipboard
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌘&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;Y&lt;/kbd&gt; Quick Look the translation in large type

Force a target language by prefixing it with `&gt;`, as in `t &gt;de Good morning`. Type `t ?` to list every supported language and whether its model is downloaded.

![Listing the available languages](images/languages.jpeg)

Translate the text selected in any app via the Universal Action. The translation is pasted over the selection, so this works best in an editable field.

![Translating a selection](images/universal-action.jpeg)

Configure the Hotkey to translate the current selection and paste the result in place, without opening Alfred.

## Workflow Configuration

Set the two languages you translate between in the Workflow's Configuration. Both directions are detected from this pair, so `en,pl` covers English to Polish and Polish to English. The keyword is configurable there as well.

Built with the help of an LLM (Claude).</string>
